  "result": "Perfect! All 104 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculation to the invoicing system.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Added lineVAT() function** to calculate VAT on the line amount after discount:\n   - VAT = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n   - Rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n   - Clamped to \u2265 0\n\n2. **Updated invoiceTotals()** to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n   - `vat` = sum of all rounded line VATs\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped to \u2265 0)\n\n3. **Updated renderInvoiceText()** to display VAT:\n   - Shows \"VAT: \u20acamount\" line when VAT > 0\n   - Shows Subtotal, Discount (if any), VAT (if any), and Total when applicable\n   - All amounts formatted via `formatEuros()`\n\n4. **Added 13 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - VAT calculation with different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - VAT on discounted amounts\n   - Mixed VAT rates across lines\n   - Rendering with VAT and without VAT\n   - Zero VAT scenarios\n\nThe implementation correctly computes VAT per line on the discounted amount, then sums the rounded line VATs\u2014never as a percentage of the invoice total.",
